    <item>
      <pubDate>Sat, 12 Sep 2026 07:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <title>Women at the Helm 2 (12 Sep 2026)</title>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;font style="font-size: 16px;"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: &amp;quot;Open Sans&amp;quot;;"&gt;&lt;img src="https://www.styc.org/resources/Pictures/e_hp_2026_wath2_1920x1080.jpg" alt="" title="" border="0"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Sloop Tavern Yacht Club is excited to announce our 7th Annual Women at the Helm Race Series. The second in the series is the Women at the Helm Regatta, a typical buoy race with the goal of completing up to three short races in the vicinity of West Point and Spring Beach.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;What makes Women at the Helm different than our other races? This series specifically requires an eligible person (please see NOR below for details) to helm through the whole race. This doesn't mean only one person can helm; in fact, we encourage crews with several eligible helmspeople to rotate through who is at the helm!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Everyone who races will receive one raffle ticket and additional tickets will be given to those who helmed, if it's your first time helming a race, and if your whole crew consists of qualifying helmspeople!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Awards and raffle will be held at The Jolly Roger Taproom at Marine Pacific/Rooftop Brewing in Ballard at 1800, with awards at 1830 and raffle afterwards.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="margin-bottom: 0px !important;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;font color="#9E0B0F" style="font-size: 24px;"&gt;UPDATE!!&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style="margin-bottom: 0px !important;"&gt;An in-person Skippers Meeting will be held on Friday, September 11 at &lt;a href="https://www.roughandtumblepub.com/ballard" target="_blank"&gt;Rough &amp;amp; Tumble&lt;/a&gt;, conveniently located in Ballard.&amp;nbsp; As one of the race sponsors, Rough &amp;amp; Tumble is donating the use of the deck with social hour starting at 5:30pm, followed by the Skippers Meeting at 7:00pm and wrapping up around 8:00pm.&amp;nbsp; A remote attendance option is also available using the link below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://meet.google.com/pzi-gxfs-emx" style="font-size: 14px;"&gt;&lt;font color="#4DBFF0"&gt;Virtual Skippers Meeting&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (7pm Friday)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A huge &lt;font color="#0054A6" face="Verdana"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THANK YOU&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&amp;nbsp;to the following for donating items to the WATH II raffle. We greatly appreciate your contributions and ongoing support!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

